// Read the trusted-stakeholder set back from a live node, and publish it on a public name.
//
// The second half of the #203 probe. Deployed as a **separate, later** deploy from `pos-trust.rho` on
// purpose: read inside the same deploy and the answer comes out of the execution overlay, where the
// write is always present — which is exactly why the defect is invisible to a single deploy and to
// every unit test that reads the state it just wrote.
//
// `getTrusted` answers a `Set`, so the newcomer's key appearing here is the whole assertion.
new pos(`rho:rchain:pos`), ret in {
  pos!("getTrusted", *ret) |
  for (@trusted <- ret) {
    @"pos-trusted"!(trusted)
  }
}
